\f1\fs22 The High Elvis and Chanta watched the Traverse station entrance from the edge of the carpark. They hadn\'92t seen any lab coats going in, or tour guides with amorous partners heading in either direction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 \'93The Holy Momma awaits,\'94 the High Elvis said.\
Chanta nodded. \'93Try not to kill anyone,\'94 he told the High Elvis, and waved the Jones clones down from the hover-pad.\
The High Elvis watched the Jones clones steal down to the station entrance with the precision of a military unit. \'93Do those guys have the same instructions?\'94\
\'93Yes.\'94\
The High Elvis signalled to the encampment north of the carpark. A band of Elvi scurried   over. Chanta eyed the guitar cases some of them were carrying. Once everyone was in position, Chanta and the High Elvis crossed the forecourt to the station entrance. Jones clones led them down the arcade ramp, and Jones clones defended the rear. At the atrium Chanta and the Jones clones advanced around the elevators and entered an emergency stairwell. The Elvi bore left into a separate stairwell. Both routes descended to the station.\
It was a long way down. Chanta wondered if he could have listened a podcast on the way to the bottom.\
The Jones clones completed their descent, Chanta following breathlessly from a dozen switchbacks above. One of the clones texted the High Elvis, saying they were in position. A minute of so later, the High Elvis texted they were ready. In the confined space, they opened the guitar cases and grabbed instruments and other items. A band of a dozen Elvi filed out and did what Elvi do best; they took the stage, beamed their smiles to their audience and wowed them with a show.\
The started with a medley of Christmas carols. Some of the guards started singing along; none had their rifles up. More Elvi took slowly to the stage, looking happy and harmless, until they\'92d formed a chorus line behind the main performers that conveniently obscured the Jones clones filing through the access corridors either side of the elevators. They crouched and ran to behind the chorus line then fanned out across the concourse, their guns with silencers drawn and aimed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 A Jones with a blue tie stepped forward. \'93You will raise your hands,\'94 he ordered when the Elvi had finished their number.\
The guards, warily raised their hands, but not too far.\
\'93We will pass. We will attend Sarah Jacobson.\'94\
\'93Sure,\'94 a guard said. \'93Present your access cards and we\'92ll get you comfortable.\'94\
\'93We will pass,\'94 the Jones said again.\
\'93I think not,\'94 the guard said. \'93We have you outgunned.\'94\
\'93Our guns are aimed and ready,\'94 the Jones said.\
\'93Ours are automatic.\'94\
Chanta pushed forward between two Joneses. \'93Hey. Guys. Come on. Put your guns away. We just need to see Sarah,\'94 he said to the guards. \'93She\'92s having a baby. Well, not right this minute, I hope, but pretty soon. I\'92m not here to hurt anybody.\'94\
\'93Present your access card,\'94 the same guard said.\
\'93Hey, I'm harmless,\'94 Chanta objected. \'93Look. Let me pass and you guys can all play cards with my guys till I get back.\'94\
The High Elvis stepped forward. \'93We Elvi are here to pay homage to the Holy Momma.\'94\
\'93The Holy Momma?\'94\
Chanta nodded and made a hurry-up gesture. \'93That\'92s Sarah too. Sarah Jacobson is the Holy Momma.\'94 \
A guard raised his rifle and aimed it at Chanta.\
A Jones fired. \'93You will check your cigarettes,\'94 he said to the guard aiming at Chanta.\
\'93What?\'94\
\'93Your cigarettes. You will inspect them.\'94\
The guard hesitated and laughed, then lowered his rifle while he retrieved his cigarettes from a cargo pocket. Flakes of tobacco fell from two neat holes on either side of the pack. There were two corresponding bullet holes in his pants.\
\'93You will release Sarah Jacobson,\'94 the lead Jones said, \'93and you will stop smoking. It\'92s bad for you.\'94\
The Elvi had been moving to either side of the concourse, which the guards took to mean they weren\'92t part of the fight; they just wanted to get out of the way. The High Elvis among them, spoke quietly and asked that the word be spread. The guitarists started playing again.\
Chanta went to them. \'93Guys. What are you doing? This wasn\'92t in the plan.\'94\
They started singing.\
