\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::2><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 What could be better than Elvis singing something like that?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 A whole bunch of Elvi singing something like that\'97that\'92s what. Regrettably, the whole performance sounds a bit much like gospel music. The bottom lips of Jones clones trembled. They dropped to their knees and laid their guns on the stone floor.\
The guards could not comprehend what they were witnessing. But when the Jones clones started sobbing, the rushed to neutralise them.\
They weren\'92t quick enough. The Elvi flanking the guards on both sides reached into the pockets. Each pulled out a small, leather disc that flash rainbow colours; each tossed in unison, and the discs spun end-over-end towards the guards.\
The guards were lifted by an energy that emerged and cohered from the discs and hurtled the guards at the feet of the Elvis and the Jones clones. At best, the could only get to their hands and knees while they tried to shake their heads clear. Some were bloodied. There may have been broken bones.\
The Elvi stopped singing; the Jones clones, still snuffling, regained a measure of composure and got to their feet. \
Chanta looked about. Relieved, he didn\'92t see anyone knocked out or dead.\
\'93Why did the Dick Tracys start crying?\'94 the High Elvis asked Chanta.\
\'93I\'85 do not know. A complete surprise.\'94 Chanta surveyed the damage. \'93I think you threw too many discs.\'94\
Where the guards had stood, the concourse was cratered. The walls had been scarred with some kind of pattern Chanta thought might be paisley.\
Worse, the one Traverse pod that had been waiting at the platform had been flipped. Chanta couldn\'92t help but think of his van, and realised he\'92d never been back to claim it. The maglev had twisted and curled up like a middle finger.\
\'93How are we supposed to get to Sarah?\'94 Chanta was distraught.\
The Elvi collected their discs and guitar cases.\
The Joneses bound the guards and inspected injuries. One of them Jumped off the platform and walk down the tunnel, found a road running for a few hundred metres parallel to the maglev tracks, and traced it back to several trucks parked in a large vehicle bay. From there, he found his way back to the Traverse concourse.
